From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotdogb bring-up <noreply@example.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-oneplus-hotdogb: fix the board compatible

The compatible string spells the board "hotdobg".  It should be
"hotdogb", which is what the OnePlus 7T is called everywhere else: the
device tree filename, the bootloader codename and the mainline board
name.

This has no functional impact today because nothing matches on it, but
it would break any driver or userspace lookup that does.

Signed-off-by: hotdogb bring-up <noreply@example.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdogb.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdogb.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdogb.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdogb.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdogb.dts
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 
 / {
 	model = "OnePlus 7T";
-	compatible = "oneplus,hotdobg", "oneplus,oneplus7", "qcom,sm8150";
+	compatible = "oneplus,hotdogb", "oneplus,oneplus7", "qcom,sm8150";
 
 	aliases {
 		display0 = &framebuffer0;

